{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Before it peoples tremble</b> — many, because of this great people. And the word פארור [gathered?] has alef, from the root פאר [with] resh doubled, like סגריר. And the meaning is that it gathers and assembles, the opposite of spreading out, like: \"gather their radiance\" [אספו נגהם]. And Dunash [Yefet] said: it is a word for blackness [שחרות], and the alef is added."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:30.105454951Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}